<SiteLayout title="Dragon Tools — Free Public Workbench" description="Useful creative and technical tools. Use the public workbench without an account; register when you want Dragon to remember, publish, collaborate or operate a space."><PublicPage active="tools" eyebrow="PUBLIC WORKBENCH" title="Come in. Make something. Leave when you're done." intro="Dragon Tools is being built as useful public infrastructure: creation tools stay approachable and free to enter; accounts add continuity, publishing and collaboration; commercial operators pay for space, scale and attention."><section class="tool-constitution"><div><b>01</b><h2>USE</h2><p>Open public tools without surrendering your project to Dragon. Local-first whenever the browser can support it.</p></div><div><b>02</b><h2>JOIN</h2><p>Register when you want saved projects, identity, collaboration, publishing, history and a place in the network.</p></div><div><b>03</b><h2>OPERATE</h2><p>Creators, shows, studios and businesses can establish persistent spaces with professional infrastructure.</p></div><div><b>04</b><h2>AMPLIFY</h2><p>Paid advertising and sponsorship buy reach. Paid placements remain clearly identified as advertising.</p></div></section><section class="tool-grid"><article><small>WRITE</small><h2>Writing Studio</h2><p>Long-form manuscripts, articles, scripts, research and structured writing.</p><span>FOUNDATION ACTIVE</span></article><article><small>VIDEO</small><h2>Video Workbench</h2><p>Cut, inspect, clip, caption and export media without making the public site a paywall maze.</p><span>PLANNED</span></article><article><small>AUDIO</small><h2>Audio / Podcast</h2><p>Podcast editing, cleanup, chapters, show publishing and broadcast workflows.</p><span>PLANNED</span></article><article><small>3D</small><h2>3D Workbench</h2><p>Model viewing and progressively deeper modeling workflows with explicit local/cloud boundaries.</p><span>PLANNED</span></article><article><small>DEV</small><h2>Developer Bench</h2><p>Code, data, conversion, game-development and inspection utilities.</p><span>PLANNED</span></article><article><small>DEVICES</small><h2>Device Bench</h2><p>Explicitly supported cameras, drones and hardware through safe browser APIs or an optional local bridge.</p><span>PLANNED</span></article></section><section class="dragon-trust"><small>DRAGON TRUST MODEL</small><h2>Your work is not the admission price.</h2><p>Anonymous tool sessions should collect only the minimum operational telemetry needed to keep Dragon reliable. Creative file contents are not silently harvested. Upload, cloud save, publishing, collaboration and account history are explicit actions.</p></section></PublicPage></SiteLayout>
